# Module 42 – AI Performance Analytics & Intelligent Service Monitoring

This module adds the operational reporting interface for HI-TECH College's AI services. It connects the usage, feedback, indexing and governance records from Modules 39–41 into one monitoring dashboard.

The module covers:

1. AI request volume, token consumption and estimated cost.
2. Usage by user, role, department, provider and model.
3. Chatbot feedback and answer-quality trends.
4. Knowledge retrieval performance.
5. Provider availability and response latency.
6. Quota threshold alerts.
7. Service health and failure monitoring.

The distinction is important: usage statistics are measurable from existing records; retrieval accuracy and answer quality require additional evaluation data. A thumbs-up rating alone is not proof that an AI answer is factually correct.

## 1. Extend the database

Add these models to `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`.

```

enum AIAlertType {
  QUOTA_WARNING
  QUOTA_EXCEEDED
  PROVIDER_FAILURE
  INDEXING_FAILURE
  HIGH_ERROR_RATE
  HIGH_LATENCY
}

enum AIAlertSeverity {
  INFO
  WARNING
  CRITICAL
}

enum AIAlertStatus {
  OPEN
  ACKNOWLEDGED
  RESOLVED
}

enum AIRetrievalOutcome {
  ANSWERED
  NO_MATCH
  LOW_CONFIDENCE
  FALLBACK
  ESCALATED
}

model AIRequestMetric {
  id              String   @id @default(uuid())
  institutionId   String
  usageRecordId   String?  @unique
  providerKey     String
  model           String
  operation       String
  latencyMs       Int?
  success         Boolean
  httpStatus      Int?
  errorCategory   String?
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([institutionId, createdAt])
  @@index([institutionId, providerKey, createdAt])
}

model AIRetrievalMetric {
  id                String             @id @default(uuid())
  institutionId     String
  conversationId    String?
  messageId         String?
  outcome           AIRetrievalOutcome
  topSimilarity     Float?
  retrievedCount    Int                @default(0)
  citedArticleIds   String[]
  createdAt         DateTime           @default(now())

  @@index([institutionId, createdAt])
  @@index([institutionId, outcome, createdAt])
}

model AIServiceAlert {
  id              String           @id @default(uuid())
  institutionId   String
  type            AIAlertType
  severity        AIAlertSeverity
  status          AIAlertStatus    @default(OPEN)
  title           String
  message         String
  source          String?
  acknowledgedById String?
  acknowledgedAt DateTime?
  resolvedById    String?
  resolvedAt      DateTime?
  createdAt       DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime         @updatedAt

  @@index([institutionId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([institutionId, type, createdAt])
}

model AIProviderHealthHistory {
  id              String   @id @default(uuid())
  institutionId   String
  providerKey     String
  healthy         Boolean
  latencyMs       Int?
  message         String?
  checkedAt       DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([institutionId, checkedAt])
  @@index([institutionId, providerKey, checkedAt])
}

```

The `AIRequestMetric.usageRecordId` is optional because failed requests may occur before a usage record is written. `AIRetrievalMetric` stores similarity measurements and retrieved article identifiers, not the entire student conversation.

